1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,250
Narrator: Listen to a podcast on health.

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:05,180
Do you have trouble sleeping at night? Then maybe this is for you.

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,940
When you worry about needing sleep and toss

4
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:10,896
and turn trying to find a comfortable position,

5
00:00:10,896 --> 00:00:13,040
you're probably only making matters worse.

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:17,140
What happens when you do that, is that your heart rate actually increases

7
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:19,200
making it more difficult to relax.

8
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,820
You may also have some bad habits that contribute to the problem

9
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:25,010
Do you rest frequently during the day?

10
00:00:25,010 --> 00:00:30,060
Do you get virtually no exercise, or do you exercise strenuously late in the day?

11
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:34,100
Are you preoccupied with sleep, or do you sleep late on weekends?

12
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:39,453
Any or all of these factors might be leading to your insomnia by disrupting your body's natural rhythm.

13
00:00:39,453 --> 00:00:42,130
What should you do, then, on those sleepless nights?

14
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:47,100
Don't bother with sleeping pills. They can actually cause worse insomnia later.

15
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:51,519
The best thing to do is drink milk or eat cheese or tuna fish.

16
00:00:51,519 --> 00:00:53,600
These are all rich in amino acids

17
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,200
and help produce a neurotransmitter in the brain that induces sleep.

18
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,860
This neurotransmitter will help you relax

19
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:03,050
and you'll be on your way to getting a good night's sleep.

20
00:01:03,050 --> 00:01:08,070
Until tomorrow's broadcast, this has been another in the series "Hints for Good Health."
